ondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le03ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Describing People "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can describe a person's appearance (the way they look)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He is well-dressed and short. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you describe someone's appearance, you talk about their: <ul><li>hair, face, skin and complexion<br> You can use these words: <span class=\"italic\">straight/wavy/curly hair, bald, beard, moustache, fair, light, dark, pale, blonde, brown, black, red</span><li> height and build<br> You can use these words: <span class=\"italic\">tall, short, thin, skinny, overweight, heavyset, muscular </span></li> <li>general appearance<br>  You can use these words: <span class=\"italic\">beautiful, well-dressed, handsome, messy, young, old</span>  </li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She has light skin and black hair."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall asleep "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to begin to sleep "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't fall asleep tonight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe people. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I'm all ears! "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "use to tell someone they have your attention "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm all ears! Tell me your story."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "creepy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "making you feel frightened  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That sounds creepy!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to wander"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to walk slowly across or around an area "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ghost wanders around the towers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to arrest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to take to a police station because the police think you have done something illegal "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: She was arrested for trying to kill him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to haunt "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to appear as a ghost in a place repeatedly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: It haunts the towers of the Kremlin."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pale "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a skin colour that is very white"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: She was a pale-faced woman."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unkempt"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not cared for or neat "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her hair was unkempt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to tremble "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to shake slightly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She looks like she is trembling."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read the story that Sally shares with Vanessa."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the same description of the woman but this time, write your own story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 7-8 lines."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your story aloud to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to their story."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can describe people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can tell a story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can listen to a story."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le03ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le03ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le03ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey Vanessa. I just sent you a message. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Shouldn't you be sleeping? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I can't fall asleep! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Why?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: My head is filled with ghost stories! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Ghost stories?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le03ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'll tell you one!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Ok! I'm all ears!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: